<FindBugsFilter>
    <!--
      EI_EXPOSE_REP / EI_EXPOSE_REP2: SpotBugs flags every getter that returns
      a mutable field, and every constructor/setter that stores a caller-
      supplied mutable reference, as a potential encapsulation break.

      This project's session/channel/config model intentionally exposes live,
      thread-safe collections (ConcurrentHashMap-backed sets, CopyOnWriteArrayList)
      directly — e.g. Channel.members()/operators()/voiced(), ClientSession's
      collections, ServerContext's registries, ServerConfiguration's parsed
      collections. These are shared, concurrently-mutated views by design
      (research.md "Message fan-out concurrency model"): defensively copying
      them on every access would both defeat their purpose (callers need to
      observe live membership/state) and cost real allocation on hot paths
      (every channel message fan-out, every registration burst). There is no
      untrusted-code boundary within jircd-core/jircd-server crossing these
      getters — this is exactly the "instances are accessed only by code
      within this project" case EI_EXPOSE_REP's own documentation names as
      the situation where the finding does not apply.
    -->
    <Match>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2" />
    </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
